From 25ef31655bfbc8e034f238d02d95c7868e960963 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 20:59:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] exynos7870: translate the gtaxlwifi comments to English

Several comments added for gtaxlwifi were written in Italian: in the
board device trees, the SoC dtsi, the G3D part of the clock driver and
the ASV fuse dump. Translate them to English, keeping their technical
content.

Many also described an earlier state of the port: U-Boot as the
bootloader, the display as the S-BOOT framebuffer only, no TMU, no CPU
DVFS, audio and cameras still to come. Bring them up to date, and
replace the status paragraph at the top of the board DTS with a short
description of the board.

Comments only: the DTBs are byte-identical and the objects differ only
in the DWARF source checksums.

Signed-off-by: Alessandro Fontana <alessandro.fontana@pm.me>
---
 .../dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dts |   90 +-
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts  | 2043 ++++++++---------
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870.dtsi    |   54 +-
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos7870.c          |   18 +-
 drivers/soc/samsung/Makefile                  |    2 +-
 drivers/soc/samsung/exynos7870-asv-dump.c     |   19 +-
 6 files changed, 1099 insertions(+), 1127 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dts
index 6dcc779095..ac65df8309 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dts
@@ -1,19 +1,15 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
 /*
  * Samsung Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2016) - SM-T580 - "gtaxlwifi"
- * Variante con il display nativo: DECON + DSI + pannello HX8279D.
+ * Variant with the native display: DECON + DSI + HX8279D panel.
  *
- * Questo file include il DTS base e ne cambia solo la parte display.
- * Tutto il resto (memoria, PMIC, eMMC, touch, batteria, pinctrl) resta
- * definito in un posto solo: se cambi il base, cambia anche questo.
+ * This file includes the base DTS and only changes its display part.
+ * Everything else (memory, PMIC, eMMC, touch, battery, pinctrl) stays
+ * defined in a single place: changing the base changes this one too.
  *
- * Il DTB base resta quello da usare finche' il pannello non funziona:
- * simpledrm e DECON attivi insieme sullo stesso buffer sono un
- * conflitto, non un ripiego. Due DTB, due voci in extlinux.conf.
- *
- * ATTENZIONE: U-Boot compila il DTS base (CONFIG_OF_LIST). Questo file
- * serve solo al kernel; non aggiungerlo alla lista di U-Boot, che non
- * ha i binding del pannello.
+ * This is the DTB the Android build ships. The base DTB, with only the
+ * simple-framebuffer, remains a fallback: simpledrm and the DECON active
+ * on the same buffer are a conflict, so a board uses one or the other.
  *
  * Copyright (C) 2026 The LineageOS Project
  */
@@ -21,8 +17,8 @@
 #include "exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts"
 
 /*
- * Via il framebuffer di S-BOOT esposto a simpledrm. Il DECON prende in
- * carico la stessa memoria attraverso memory-region, qui sotto.
+ * Drop the S-BOOT framebuffer exposed to simpledrm. The DECON takes over
+ * the same memory through memory-region, below.
  */
 /delete-node/ &framebuffer0;
 
@@ -30,14 +26,14 @@ / {
 	model = "Samsung Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2016) (DECON)";
 
 	/*
-	 * Alimentazione del pannello, lato "alto". Il downstream
-	 * (decon_board, gpio_buck_en) accende un DC-DC esterno con
-	 * gpd3-4 e aspetta 15 ms; non e' un LDO del PMIC.
+	 * Panel supply, "high" side. Downstream (decon_board,
+	 * gpio_buck_en) switches on an external DC-DC with gpd3-4 and
+	 * waits 15 ms; it is not a PMIC LDO.
 	 *
-	 * DA CONFERMARE: la tensione reale. Il valore qui serve solo a
-	 * soddisfare regulator_is_supported_voltage() nel driver, che
-	 * pretende vdd fra 3,0 e 5,0 V; non viene programmato nulla,
-	 * il regolatore e' un semplice interruttore su GPIO.
+	 * TO BE CONFIRMED: the actual voltage. The value here only
+	 * satisfies regulator_is_supported_voltage() in the driver,
+	 * which wants vdd between 3.0 and 5.0 V; nothing is programmed,
+	 * the regulator is a plain GPIO switch.
 	 */
 	lcd_buck: regulator-lcd-buck {
 		compatible = "regulator-fixed";
@@ -55,16 +51,16 @@ lcd_buck: regulator-lcd-buck {
 };
 
 /*
- * Handoff dal framebuffer del bootloader, meccanismo preso da
- * exynos7870-j6lte.dts: la regione riservata resta no-map e in piu'
- * dichiara l'identity mapping nell'IOMMU del DECON, cosi' il blocco non
- * fa page fault fra il probe e il primo modeset.
+ * Handoff from the bootloader framebuffer, mechanism taken from
+ * exynos7870-j6lte.dts: the reserved region stays no-map and also
+ * declares the identity mapping in the DECON IOMMU, so the block does
+ * not page fault between probe and the first modeset.
  *
- * fb_mem e' gia' definito nel DTS base a 0x67000000 con la dimensione
- * giusta: qui basta aggiungere la proprieta'.
+ * fb_mem is already defined in the base DTS at 0x67000000 with the
+ * right size: adding the property here is enough.
  *
- * Dopo la compilazione ricontrolla il risultato, che la sintassi di
- * iommu-addresses e' facile da sbagliare in silenzio:
+ * Check the result after compiling, as the iommu-addresses syntax is
+ * easy to get silently wrong:
  *   dtc -I dtb -O dts exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dtb | grep -A3 iommu-add
  */
 &fb_mem {
@@ -78,12 +74,12 @@ &decon {
 };
 
 /*
- * samsung-dsim ricava PMS da burst-clock-frequency. Il downstream
- * dichiara pms = <3 226 1> con riferimento a 26 MHz, che da'
- * 26 x 226 / (3 x 2^1) = 979,3 MHz: coerente con i 980 Mbps/lane del
- * nodo hx8279d_wuxga (timing,dsi-hs-clk = 980).
+ * samsung-dsim derives PMS from burst-clock-frequency. Downstream
+ * declares pms = <3 226 1> with a 26 MHz reference, which gives
+ * 26 x 226 / (3 x 2^1) = 979.3 MHz: consistent with the 980 Mbps/lane
+ * of the hx8279d_wuxga node (timing,dsi-hs-clk = 980).
  *
- * 980 Mbps x 4 lane = 3,92 Gbps contro i 3,83 richiesti a 24 bpp.
+ * 980 Mbps x 4 lanes = 3.92 Gbps against the 3.83 needed at 24 bpp.
  */
 &dsi {
 	#address-cells = <1>;
@@ -100,17 +96,17 @@ panel@0 {
 		reg = <0>;
 
 		/*
-		 * vdd  = DC-DC esterno su gpd3-4  (buck_en downstream)
-		 * iovcc = LDO35 del PMIC, "LCD_1P8" a 1,8 V
+		 * vdd  = external DC-DC on gpd3-4  (buck_en downstream)
+		 * iovcc = PMIC LDO35, "LCD_1P8" at 1.8 V
 		 */
 		vdd-supply = <&lcd_buck>;
 		iovcc-supply = <&vdd_ldo35>;
 
 		/*
-		 * Il driver porta reset_gpio a 1 e SUBITO DOPO parla in
-		 * DSI: in questo driver il valore logico 1 significa
-		 * "reset rilasciato". Il downstream rilascia portando il
-		 * pin alto, quindi ACTIVE_HIGH.
+		 * The driver sets reset_gpio to 1 and RIGHT AFTER talks
+		 * DSI: in this driver logical 1 means "reset released".
+		 * Downstream releases it by driving the pin high, hence
+		 * ACTIVE_HIGH.
 		 */
 		reset-gpios = <&gpd4 1 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 
@@ -120,21 +116,21 @@ panel@0 {
 };
 
 /*
- * Ora il pannello ha un consumatore vero: il regolatore non deve piu'
- * restare acceso per forza, altrimenti unprepare() non spegne niente e
- * i ~230 mA a schermo spento restano.
+ * The panel now has a real consumer: the regulator must no longer be
+ * forced on, otherwise unprepare() switches nothing off and the ~230 mA
+ * with the screen off remain.
  */
 &vdd_ldo35 {
 	/delete-property/ regulator-always-on;
 };
 
 /*
- * gpd3 e gpd4 stanno sotto pinctrl_top, come bt_enable ("gpd4-0") e
- * wlan_enable ("gpd3-6") nel J6.
+ * gpd3 and gpd4 sit under pinctrl_top, like bt_enable ("gpd4-0") and
+ * wlan_enable ("gpd3-6") on the J6.
  *
- * Nessun samsung,pin-val: i pin arrivano gia' configurati da S-BOOT col
- * pannello acceso, e il driver li prende con GPIOD_ASIS proprio per non
- * interrompere l'immagine del bootloader prima del primo modeset.
+ * No samsung,pin-val: the pins come already configured by S-BOOT with
+ * the panel on, and the driver takes them with GPIOD_ASIS precisely so
+ * as not to interrupt the bootloader image before the first modeset.
  */
 &pinctrl_top {
 	lcd_rst: lcd-rst-pins {
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts
index f1c6e73e16..705514eabf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-gtaxlwifi.dts
@@ -3,24 +3,19 @@
  * Samsung Galaxy Tab A 10.1 (2016) - SM-T580 - codename "gtaxlwifi"
  * SoC: Exynos 7870 (Joshua)
  *
- * Stato: dispositivo autonomo. eMMC, USB gadget, touchscreen, tasti, GPU
- * (Panfrost), PMIC, ADC del SoC e catena batteria completa (fuel gauge,
- * charger, MUIC) funzionano. Il display e' ancora il framebuffer lasciato
- * acceso da S-BOOT via simpledrm: niente DECON/DSI, niente backlight.
- * Entrambi i banchi di RAM sono dichiarati (vedi memory@ qui sotto).
- * Fotocamera anteriore (SR259 su CSIS1) in fondo, la posteriore
- * non ancora. Sensori: accelerometro LIS2HH12 su i2c7
- * dichiarato con mount-matrix misurata (senza IRQ), piu' il sensore
- * di luce CM3323 sullo stesso bus (vedi in fondo). Audio in lavorazione:
- * catena completa dichiarata (lpass, adma, i2s0, mixer s1402x,
- * codec RT5659 su i2c5, scheda sound); collaudo del primo suono in
- * corso. Manca la cattura (mic differenziali, jack detection).
- *
- * Basato su arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-j6lte.dts
- * (Kaustabh Chakraborty, mainline dal ciclo 6.16)
- *
- * Questo file e' compilato sia dal kernel sia da U-Boot: ogni macro o
- * label nuova deve esistere anche nella copia dei binding dentro U-Boot.
+ * Wi-Fi only 10.1" tablet with 2 GiB of RAM in two banks, eMMC, microSD,
+ * QCA9377 Wi-Fi (SDIO) and Bluetooth (UART), BCM4752 GPS, S2MPU05 PMIC,
+ * SM5703 charger, fuel gauge and MUIC, STMicro FTS touchscreen, keys and
+ * Hall sensor, Mali-T830 GPU, LIS2HH12 accelerometer, CM3323 light sensor,
+ * front (SR259) and rear (S5K4H5YC) cameras, and audio through the
+ * s1402x mixer and a Realtek RT5659 codec (playback and internal mic).
+ *
+ * This file describes the display as the framebuffer left on by S-BOOT;
+ * exynos7870-gtaxlwifi-decon.dts includes it and replaces that with the
+ * DECON, DSI and the HX8279D panel with backlight.
+ *
+ * Based on arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-j6lte.dts
+ * (Kaustabh Chakraborty, mainline since the 6.16 cycle)
  *
  * Copyright (C) 2026 The LineageOS Project
  */
@@ -39,17 +34,17 @@ / {
 
 	/*
 	 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
-	 * PROPRIETA' NON-STANDARD LETTE DA dtbhtoolExynos
+	 * NON-STANDARD PROPERTIES READ BY dtbhtoolExynos
 	 * ------------------------------------------------------------------
-	 * exynos7870.dtsi dichiara GIA' model_info-chip = <7870>,
-	 * model_info-hw_rev = <0> e model_info-hw_rev_end = <255>, con il
-	 * commento "Stock Samsung bootloader looks for these properties".
-	 * Sono esattamente i valori che servono: non li ridichiaro.
+	 * exynos7870.dtsi ALREADY declares model_info-chip = <7870>,
+	 * model_info-hw_rev = <0> and model_info-hw_rev_end = <255>, with the
+	 * comment "Stock Samsung bootloader looks for these properties".
+	 * Those are exactly the values needed: they are not repeated here.
 	 *
-	 * Mancano pero' platform e subtype, che nessun DTS mainline definisce.
-	 * dtbhtoolExynos li converte nei codici dell'header DTBH; i valori
-	 * qui sotto sono quelli che producono 0x50a6 / 0x217584da, estratti
-	 * dal boot.img funzionante di LineageOS.
+	 * Platform and subtype are missing, though, and no mainline DTS
+	 * defines them. dtbhtoolExynos turns them into the DTBH header codes;
+	 * the values below are the ones that produce 0x50a6 / 0x217584da,
+	 * taken from a working LineageOS boot.img.
 	 */
 	model_info-platform = "android";
 	model_info-subtype = "samsung";
@@ -65,44 +60,44 @@ aliases {
 
 	chosen {
 		/*
-		 * Confermato: exynos7870.dtsi usa #address-cells = <2> /
-		 * #size-cells = <1>, come exynos850 e exynos7885. Tutti i reg
-		 * di questo file seguono quel formato: due celle di indirizzo
-		 * (la prima e' sempre 0, la RAM sta sotto i 4 GB) e una sola
-		 * cella di dimensione, che basta fino a 4 GB per regione.
+		 * Confirmed: exynos7870.dtsi uses #address-cells = <2> /
+		 * #size-cells = <1>, like exynos850 and exynos7885. Every reg
+		 * in this file follows that format: two address cells (the
+		 * first is always 0, RAM is below 4 GB) and a single size
+		 * cell, which is enough for up to 4 GB per region.
 		 */
 		#address-cells = <2>;
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges;
 
 		/*
-		 * ttySAC2 e' la console di debug su tutta la famiglia 7870, ed e'
-		 * confermata dal cmdline stock: androidboot.sec_atd.tty=/dev/ttySAC2
-		 * Con "earlycon" (senza argomenti) nel cmdline il kernel usa
-		 * automaticamente questo nodo, il che ti da' output seriale
-		 * prima ancora che il framebuffer sia inizializzato.
+		 * ttySAC2 is the debug console across the whole 7870 family, as
+		 * confirmed by the stock cmdline: androidboot.sec_atd.tty=/dev/ttySAC2
+		 * With "earlycon" (no arguments) on the cmdline the kernel uses
+		 * this node automatically, which gives serial output even
+		 * before the framebuffer is initialized.
 		 */
 		stdout-path = &serial2;
 
 		/*
-		 * Framebuffer lasciato attivo da S-BOOT.
-		 * L'indirizzo viene dal cmdline stock: s3cfb.bootloaderfb=0x67000000
-		 * (identico al J6, al J7 Prime e all'A2 Core: S-BOOT lo mette
-		 * sempre li' su questo SoC).
+		 * Framebuffer left active by S-BOOT.
+		 * The address comes from the stock cmdline: s3cfb.bootloaderfb=0x67000000
+		 * (same as on the J6, J7 Prime and A2 Core: S-BOOT always puts
+		 * it there on this SoC).
 		 *
-		 * CONFERMATO dal DTS downstream, exynos7870-gtaxl_common.dtsi:
+		 * CONFIRMED by the downstream DTS, exynos7870-gtaxl_common.dtsi:
 		 *   decon_fb@14830000 { bootloader_fb = <0x67000000 0 0 1200 1920 0>; }
-		 * e da sysfs sul dispositivo acceso:
+		 * and by sysfs on the running device:
 		 *   virtual_size   = 1200,1920
-		 *   stride         = 4800   (= 1200*4, nessun padding di riga)
+		 *   stride         = 4800   (= 1200*4, no line padding)
 		 *   bits_per_pixel = 32
 		 *
-		 * Nessun double buffering. Il DECON fa lo scanout in PORTRAIT
-		 * anche se il pannello e' un 10.1" landscape: il pannello
-		 * (Himax HX8279D, 135x216 mm) e' montato ruotato di 90 gradi.
-		 * La console apparira' quindi ruotata; si corregge da cmdline
-		 * con fbcon=rotate:1 (oppure :3), non toccando questi numeri,
-		 * che descrivono la memoria e sono corretti cosi'.
+		 * No double buffering. The DECON scans out in PORTRAIT even
+		 * though the panel is a 10.1" landscape one: the panel
+		 * (Himax HX8279D, 135x216 mm) is mounted rotated by 90 degrees.
+		 * The console therefore shows up rotated; fix that on the
+		 * cmdline with fbcon=rotate:1 (or :3), not by touching these
+		 * numbers, which describe the memory and are correct as they are.
 		 */
 		framebuffer0: framebuffer@67000000 {
 			compatible = "simple-framebuffer";
@@ -115,30 +110,30 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer@67000000 {
 	};
 
 	/*
-	 * Layout REALE, da exynos7870-gtaxl_common.dtsi (righe 22-30).
-	 * Il downstream dichiara DUE banchi con un buco in mezzo:
+	 * ACTUAL layout, from exynos7870-gtaxl_common.dtsi (lines 22-30).
+	 * Downstream declares TWO banks with a hole in between:
 	 *
-	 *   banco 1: 0x40000000 + 0x3E400000  -> fino a 0x7E400000
-	 *   [ BUCO:  0x7E400000 .. 0x80000000 = 28 MB, TrustZone/secure ]
-	 *   banco 2: 0x80000000 + 0x40000000  -> fino a 0xC0000000
+	 *   bank 1: 0x40000000 + 0x3E400000  -> up to 0x7E400000
+	 *   [ HOLE: 0x7E400000 .. 0x80000000 = 28 MB, TrustZone/secure ]
+	 *   bank 2: 0x80000000 + 0x40000000  -> up to 0xC0000000
 	 *
-	 * Totale 0x7E400000 = ~2020 MB, coerente con MemTotal 1994048 kB
-	 * una volta tolto l'overhead del kernel.
+	 * Total 0x7E400000 = ~2020 MB, consistent with MemTotal 1994048 kB
+	 * once the kernel overhead is taken out.
 	 *
-	 * Entrambi i banchi sono dichiarati. Nel banco 2 vive la ECT
-	 * (Exynos Character Table, parametri DVFS depositati dal bootloader
-	 * a 0x90000000, 0x14000 byte): e' riservata no-map nel blocco
-	 * reserved-memory qui sotto, altrimenti l'allocatore ci scrive
-	 * sopra appena il banco 2 diventa disponibile.
+	 * Both banks are declared. Bank 2 holds the ECT (Exynos Character
+	 * Table, DVFS parameters left by the bootloader at 0x90000000,
+	 * 0x14000 bytes): it is reserved no-map in the reserved-memory
+	 * block below, otherwise the allocator writes over it as soon as
+	 * bank 2 becomes available.
 	 *
-	 * ATTENZIONE al buco: NON accorpare i due banchi in un unico range
-	 * 0x40000000..0xC0000000. I 28 MB in mezzo non sono RAM utilizzabile
-	 * e mapparli produce un external abort senza log leggibili. E'
-	 * l'unica ragione per cui i nodi restano due: non unificarli.
+	 * MIND the hole: do NOT merge the two banks into a single range
+	 * 0x40000000..0xC0000000. The 28 MB in between are not usable RAM
+	 * and mapping them causes an external abort with no readable log.
+	 * That is the only reason the nodes stay two: do not merge them.
 	 *
-	 * Attesa dopo la dichiarazione di entrambi i banchi: la riga
-	 * "Memory: ...K/2068480K available" nel dmesg (2020 MiB), contro
-	 * 1019904K con il solo banco 1.
+	 * Expected with both banks declared: the line
+	 * "Memory: ...K/2068480K available" in dmesg (2020 MiB), against
+	 * 1019904K with bank 1 alone.
 	 */
 	memory@40000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
@@ -151,12 +146,12 @@ memory@80000000 {
 	};
 
 	/*
-	 * Dati di targa della cella, letti dal fuel gauge tramite
-	 * monitored-battery. Da exynos7870-gtaxlwifi_eur_open_battery_05.dtsi:
+	 * Cell ratings, read by the fuel gauge through monitored-battery.
+	 * From exynos7870-gtaxlwifi_eur_open_battery_05.dtsi:
 	 *   battery,battery_full_capacity = <7300>   (mAh)
-	 *   battery0,battery_type = <4350>           (mV, tensione massima)
-	 * La tensione minima e' la soglia di cut-off usata dal downstream
-	 * (battery0,tem_poff, primo valore).
+	 *   battery0,battery_type = <4350>           (mV, maximum voltage)
+	 * The minimum voltage is the cut-off threshold used downstream
+	 * (battery0,tem_poff, first value).
 	 */
 	battery: battery {
 		compatible = "simple-battery";
@@ -166,41 +161,42 @@ battery: battery {
 		voltage-min-design-microvolt = <3400000>;
 
 		/*
-		 * Parametri di ricarica, dal downstream:
+		 * Charging parameters, from downstream:
 		 *   battery,chg_float_voltage = <4300>
-		 *   battery,fast_charging_current: 2400 mA per il caricatore
-		 *     da parete (primo elemento della tabella per tipo di cavo)
+		 *   battery,fast_charging_current: 2400 mA for the wall
+		 *     charger (first entry of the per-cable-type table)
 		 *   battery,full_check_current_1st = <375>
-		 * La tensione di float scende con l'invecchiamento della cella
-		 * (battery,age_data downstream); qui resta il valore per cella
-		 * nuova, perche' mainline non tiene il conteggio dei cicli.
+		 * The float voltage goes down as the cell ages (battery,age_data
+		 * downstream); this keeps the value for a new cell, because
+		 * mainline does not keep a cycle count.
 		 */
 		constant-charge-voltage-max-microvolt = <4300000>;
 		constant-charge-current-max-microamp = <2400000>;
 		charge-term-current-microamp = <375000>;
 
 		/*
-		 * Fuori da questo intervallo il charger smette di caricare, e
-		 * riprende 5 gradi dentro; il fuel gauge riporta Overheat o
-		 * Cold. Dal downstream: battery,temp_high_threshold_normal =
-		 * <500> (recovery 450) e battery,temp_low_threshold_normal =
-		 * <0> (recovery 50), in decimi di grado. Nel chip nessuno
-		 * guarda la cella: la sua regolazione termica e' per il die.
+		 * Outside this range the charger stops charging, and resumes
+		 * 5 degrees inside it; the fuel gauge reports Overheat or
+		 * Cold. From downstream: battery,temp_high_threshold_normal =
+		 * <500> (recovery 450) and battery,temp_low_threshold_normal =
+		 * <0> (recovery 50), in tenths of a degree. Nothing in the chip
+		 * watches the cell: its thermal regulation is for the die.
 		 */
 		operating-range-celsius = <0 50>;
 	};
 
 	/*
-	 * Termistore della batteria. Non e' nel fuel gauge: quello misura la
-	 * temperatura del proprio die, che a riposo legge una ventina di
-	 * gradi piu' del pacco. Il termistore vero e' letto dall'ADC del SoC
-	 * sul canale 1 (downstream: io-channel-names = "adc-temp").
+	 * Battery thermistor. It is not in the fuel gauge: that one measures
+	 * the temperature of its own die, which at rest reads some twenty
+	 * degrees above the pack. The real thermistor is read by the SoC ADC
+	 * on channel 1 (downstream: io-channel-names = "adc-temp").
 	 *
-	 * La tabella e' battery,temp_table_adc / battery,temp_table_data da
